non-constant q: min relative gap to lower 1.12e-06, to upper 1.16e-03 (strict)
constant q: max rel |R0 - beta q/gamma| = 9.47e-15
  symmetric : n=477, normalised position (R0-lo)/(hi-lo): min 0.001 median 0.199 max 0.792
  departure : n=500, normalised position (R0-lo)/(hi-lo): min 0.000 median 0.299 max 0.848
  nonrev    : n=508, normalised position (R0-lo)/(hi-lo): min 0.002 median 0.243 max 0.951
  dense     : n=511, normalised position (R0-lo)/(hi-lo): min 0.000 median 0.039 max 0.509
== Theorem 3: mobility limits, monotonicity, asymptotics ==
instances 300; max increase of R0 between successive D (relative) = 2.65e-12 (<=0 up to rounding)
strict-decrease failures (non-constant q): 0
D->inf: max rel |R0 - beta<q>_pi/gamma| = 3.76e-06;  D->0: max rel |R0 - beta q_max/gamma| = 2.57e-07
growth rate lambda1(D): max violation of convexity / monotonicity = 1.30e-15
large-D expansion error ratio err(30 s_L)/err(300 s_L): median 99.9 (expect 100), [98.4, 102.0] (n=227)
small-D expansion error ratio err(0.01 s_S)/err(0.001 s_S): median 99.5 (expect 100), [96.4, 101.0] (n=299)
-- Theorem 3': edge-wise monotonicity (symmetric) and zone lower bound
symmetric: raising one edge rate, max rel increase of R0 over 900 trials = 7.27e-16 (<= 0)
departure model: raising D at one cell -> R0 up in 201, down in 98 of 300 trials (no monotonicity)
zone bound beta q_Z/(gamma+mu_Z) <= R0: max rel violation over 878 random zones = 0.00e+00
